{"labs": [{"id": 0, "type": "scholar", "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "id": 0}, {"id": 2, "title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"text": "", "id": 0, "time": "0", "image": ""}, {"text": "Can you tell me who the most popular animal TV star is? You must be astounded to know that the cute animals that we see in movies and on television do not have an easy life either. In some cases, animal stars have been beaten and have not been given food so that they will perform the way the trainers want them to. In addition, although American law does not allow animals to be killed on film, other countries do not seem to mind.", "id": 1, "time": "100", "image": ""}, {"text": "You must be relieved to hear that there has been a big push toward animal rights in the last decade or so. Activists have called attention to the issue of animal abuse. This has resulted in a gradual shift away from using animals in TV shows - or at least toward better conditions for those that remain in the industry.", "id": 2, "time": "25200", "image": ""}, {"text": "So the next time you are watching an animal perform and you find yourself enjoying the show, you might want to stop and think. That very animal may be a victim of mistreatment and abuse. Where did we go wrong as people?", "id": 3, "time": "43000", "image": ""}], "video_src": "engenn7le12ob02re2vid01"}, "type": "video"}], "_data": [], "type": "video", "template_override": 1}], "exercises": [{"id": 0, "type": "WLC", "questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "  I can talk about nature and the animal world.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "  I can show I understand someone's feelings. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "  I can ask for clarification or use rhetorical questions to emphasize a point.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "  What animals are considered \u201cstars\u201d in your country? Why? ", "type": "Free